### Interpretations
1. [derived from Facts 10,16,26,27,28,29] The candidate runs (with only the Narrative user prompt changed) coincided with lower mean scores for both Narrative and Compose compared with the reused baseline runs.

### Unknowns
- Whether the added section titled "Preserve Editorial Intent from the Synthesis" was the cause of the observed editorial drift rather than some other factor.
- Which exact wording, clause, or phrasing in the added section (if any) produced the observed changes in model behaviour.
- Whether the observed drift would occur with more than three runs per condition or with temperature/seed control.
- Whether the model alias `gpt-5-mini` mapped to a different backend between baseline and candidate runs.
- Whether changes outside the Narrative user prompt (including transient model provider behavior) contributed to the observed differences.
- Whether the internal tension in the baseline Synthesis (company identity present alongside a later description calling orchestration "central to the product direction") causally influenced candidate outputs.
- Whether a revised or more specific preservation instruction would avoid the regressions observed here.
- Whether the experiment's results generalize to other content formats, other prompts, or other model families.
- Quantitative statistical significance of the score differences beyond descriptive means and sample SDs.

